# Testing

- Backend: Jest 30 + Supertest. Tests in `backend/tests/{unit,api}`.
  - Every endpoint needs an API test (happy path + auth/authorization failure).
  - Pure helpers (`utils/`, price math, status transitions, validators) need unit tests.
  - API tests build the app via `createApp({ prisma: mockPrisma })` — never hit a real DB.
- Frontend: Vitest 5 + React Testing Library 16 (jsdom).
  - Test files live next to the source: `src/**/__tests__/*.test.ts(x)`.
  - Test pure helpers, Zustand stores, and components with meaningful logic
    (forms, validation, status trackers).
  - Mock `helpers/api.ts` with `vi.mock` — tests never hit the network.
- Commands (run from repo root before finishing):
  `npm test`, `npm run lint`, `npm run typecheck`.
- New feature = tests first or at least alongside. Coverage must not drop.
